# Output of scripts/simulate-az-failover.sh, AWS Academy Learner Lab (us-east-1), 19 Nov 2026 (times UTC).
# Each run forces an RDS Multi-AZ failover (aws rds reboot-db-instance --force-failover) while
# polling GET /api/health?deep=1 (API Gateway -> Lambda -> PostgreSQL SELECT 1) every ~3 s.
# HTTP 000 = request timed out after 5 s (shown as "000000" with the previous response by the first
# script version; fixed afterwards).
#
# Summary - outage = last successful check before the failure to first successful check after it:
#   run 1: 11:39:27 -> 11:39:43  <= 16 s   primary us-east-1b -> us-east-1a (AZ reported a few minutes later)
#   run 2: 11:44:19 -> 11:44:33  <= 14 s   primary us-east-1a -> us-east-1b
#   run 3: 11:48:51 -> 11:49:08  <= 17 s   primary us-east-1b -> us-east-1a
# Result: worst case under 20 seconds against a 1-hour RTO; synchronous standby, so no committed data lost.

